  "body": "This really should live in your own application logic.\n\n> Currently, developers can manually inspect openDialogs or use getDialogById() before opening a dialog.\n\nJust keep track of a ref, clear it on dialog close, and don't open a dialog if the ref already exists. Also forces you to think what should happen if same dialog class were to be opened with different arguments multiple times.",
